## 1. Research and Educational Use Only

NeuroScan AI is an experimental software project intended for research, education, software development, and technical evaluation. It has not been established as a clinically validated medical device.

## 2. No Medical Advice or Diagnosis

The software, its source code, models, predictions, classifications, segmentation masks, visualizations, confidence scores, and other outputs are provided for informational and experimental purposes only. They do not constitute medical advice, a professional radiological interpretation, or a diagnosis of any disease or medical condition.

## 3. No Clinical Reliance

Do not use NeuroScan AI as the sole or decisive basis for diagnosing, screening, excluding, monitoring, or treating a medical condition, or for making decisions concerning patient care. Do not delay or avoid professional medical evaluation based on any output from this project. All medical decisions must be made by appropriately qualified healthcare professionals using independent clinical judgment and suitable clinical evidence.

## 4. No Guarantee of Accuracy

The software may produce incorrect, incomplete, inconsistent, misleading, or unreliable results, including false-positive and false-negative findings. Performance may vary with image quality, MRI acquisition protocols, patient populations, preprocessing, model weights, software configuration, and other factors. Experimental evaluation results do not establish clinical safety, effectiveness, generalizability, or regulatory approval.

## 5. No Clinical Validation or Regulatory Authorization

Unless expressly documented otherwise in a verifiable written authorization, the project has not been validated or authorized for clinical use by a competent regulatory authority. Users are responsible for determining whether their intended use requires clinical validation, regulatory authorization, professional oversight, or compliance with applicable laws.

